   "description": "Khung môn học theo syllabus FLM chính thức.",
   "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">CDP301 · Section 0 · Lesson 0.6</span>\n<h2>Student tasks & constructive questions</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">The rules you are held to (attendance, preparation, exam eligibility) — verbatim.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM · Syllabus ID 14386 · Decision 968/QĐ-ĐHFPT dated 07/08/2026 · collected 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">CDP301 · Mục 0 · Bài 0.6</span>\n<h2>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên & câu hỏi kiến tạo</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">Những quy định bạn phải tuân theo (chuyên cần, chuẩn bị bài, điều kiện dự thi) — nguyên văn.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: FLM · Syllabus ID 14386 · QĐ 968/QĐ-ĐHFPT ngày 07/08/2026 · thu ngày 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student tasks (verbatim)</h3>\n<p>Students are expected to:<br><br>- Students must attend at least 80% of contact sessions in order to be accepted to the final examination.<br><br>- Attend and participate actively in lectures, labs, and discussions according to the weekly schedule<br><br>- Complete all project milestones, including:<br><br>- Collaborate effectively in teams, including task allocation, maintaining project logs, and performing peer reviews of other teams’ designs<br><br>- Engage in self-directed learning by exploring components, IoT modules, and best practices in EMC/EMI and layout optimization<br><br>- Deliver and present the Final Project, including a functional PCB prototype, working firmware, a comprehensive technical report, and a live or recorded demonstration</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên (nguyên văn)</h3>\n<p>Students are expected to:<br><br>- Students must attend at least 80% of contact sessions in order to be accepted to the final examination.<br><br>- Attend and participate actively in lectures, labs, and discussions according to the weekly schedule<br><br>- Complete all project milestones, including:<br><br>- Collaborate effectively in teams, including task allocation, maintaining project logs, and performing peer reviews of other teams’ designs<br><br>- Engage in self-directed learning by exploring components, IoT modules, and best practices in EMC/EMI and layout optimization<br><br>- Deliver and present the Final Project, including a functional PCB prototype, working firmware, a comprehensive technical report, and a live or recorded demonstration</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Everything in the tables above is copied <strong>verbatim</strong> from the university's FLM page (in English, as published) so you can check it against the copy your lecturer gives you: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14386\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14386</a> (needs your FPT login). If FLM publishes a newer syllabus, FLM wins.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Mọi thứ trong các bảng trên được chép <strong>nguyên văn</strong> từ trang FLM của trường (bằng tiếng Anh, đúng như trường công bố) để bạn đối chiếu với bản giảng viên phát: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14386\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=14386</a> (cần đăng nhập tài khoản FPT). Nếu FLM công bố bản syllabus mới hơn thì theo FLM.</div></div>"
